  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Marc Marquez, a prominent figure in motorcycle racing and an eight-time world champion, has officially announced his retirement from MotoGP, effective after the conclusion of the 2026 season. The athlete cited reaching his physical limits as a primary factor in this career decision, noting that complications from diplopia—which resurfaced following significant crashes at the Mandalika and Le Mans circuits—have made continued competition unsustainable. The announcement has prompted widespread discussion within the MotoGP paddock, particularly regarding the future of the Ducati team. With a vacancy opening on the roster, the organization is currently identifying successors to fill his position, with reports naming Fermin Aldeguer as a leading candidate and Nicolo Bulega as a potential alternative. This transition marks the conclusion of a significant chapter in the sport's recent history, following his competitive performances at venues such as the Ricardo Tormo circuit.",
